  "description": "CR 701.40g a manifested SORCERY stays face down, and still deals a 2/2's damage",
  "note": "CR 701.40g is reachable only through an effect: neither CR 708.7 procedure can propose turning up an instant or sorcery card. Showstopping Surprise turns the chosen creature face up if it's face down, then it deals damage equal to its power to each other creature, which turns the rule into a number. Soul Summons manifests the top card. Armored Galleon, a 5/4, survives both the face-down 2/2's 2 and a face-up Hill Giant's 3, so its damage is read rather than a death inferred. Prey Upon is under the manifest, so it stays a face-down 2/2 creature and the Galleon takes 2; turned up, it would be a sorcery permanent with no power.",
